What is Service Discovery?

Service Discovery is the process of automatically detecting services in a network so 
that microservices can communicate without hardcoding addresses.

Types of Service Discovery
Has Tow Types of service discovery mechanisms:

Client-Side Service Discovery
The client (consumer service) queries a Service Registry to get the location (IP, Port) of the required service.

Example: Netflix Eureka, Consul

No load on the service registry after discovery.

Server-Side Service Discovery
The client sends a request to a Load Balancer (e.g., API Gateway, Kubernetes Service).

Example: AWS ALB (Application Load Balancer), Kubernetes Service

Clients don’t need to handle discovery logic.
Centralized load balancing.